From: cezanne port
Subject: [PATCH] boot-splash: flush the displays when the splash becomes idle

The displays stay paused while the splash is shown and on_new_frame
flushes them every frame tick. Becoming idle for a deactivate, two-step
without an end animation stops the throbber (drawn away, not flushed),
the idle handler drops DRM master 10 ms later: the last throbber frame
stays on screen (GDM deactivates plymouth at its start).
---
diff --git a/src/libply-splash-core/ply-boot-splash.c b/src/libply-splash-core/ply-boot-splash.c
--- a/src/libply-splash-core/ply-boot-splash.c
+++ b/src/libply-splash-core/ply-boot-splash.c
@@ -775,6 +775,11 @@
 on_idle (ply_boot_splash_t *splash)
 {
         ply_trace ("splash now idle");
+        /* The plugin may have drawn its final state (e.g. erased a stopped
+         * throbber) since the last frame tick, and the idle handler can
+         * deactivate the renderer before the next tick would flush it.
+         */
+        ply_boot_splash_flush_displays (splash);
         ply_event_loop_watch_for_timeout (splash->loop, 0.01,
                                           (ply_event_loop_timeout_handler_t)
                                           splash->idle_handler,
